meta {
  name: Close Run
  type: http
  seq: 37
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/close
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 201", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("the run is closed, and says by whom", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconRunId"));
    expect(body.closedAt).to.be.a("string");
    expect(body.closedBy).to.be.an("object");
    expect(body.closedBy.name).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/close — close a month

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation`
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:write`

  Takes the month's rows off every assignee's list ("Assigned to me", the
  Producer Dashboard's Dash follow-ups), and off work transfer and release,
  until it is reopened. While closed, none of its rows can be handed to
  anyone (`PATCH …/assignment` answers 409; taking a row back still works).

  Nothing is decided or deleted: the owner still reads, decides and re-checks
  the rows here, and assignments are kept, so `Reopen Run` puts each open row
  back with whoever had it. A re-upload of a closed month stays closed.

  Without closing, every month ever uploaded stays its period's current run,
  so its open rows stayed on people's lists for good (PAC-173 review).

  Idempotent: closing a closed month answers the run unchanged.

  ## Response `201`

  The run (`ReconciliationRunDetail`) with `closedAt` (ISO instant) and
  `closedBy` (`{ id, name }`). Both are `null` on an open run.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — `:id` is not an ObjectId
  - `403` — no `carrier_reconciliation:write`
  - `404` — no such run in the agency
  - `409` — a re-upload replaced the run (close the month on the new one), or
    the run did not finish
}
